q('OR100','Procedure Pass',[71,83],'A nurse wants to focus on pre-surgical tasks assigned to their role. Which approach is most direct?', ['Use the Tasks section grouped by role','Post the log to filter the tasks','Remove the case from the schedule','Open a surgeon preference list'],[0],'Procedure Pass tasks can be grouped by role. Posting, unscheduling, and order preference lists do not provide that task view.')
q('OR100','Preference tools',[40,49,114],'A surgeon wants to place several related orders together during one ordering session. Which tool fits?', ['Order set','Preference card','OR block','Surgical log'],[0],'An order set groups related orders for ordering. A preference card configures surgical preferences; a block reserves time; a log records actual surgery.')
q('OR100','Inventory',[104,105],'Which items belong to the pick-list content described in the course? Select all that apply.', ['Medications','Supplies','Named circulating nurses','Individually assigned equipment'],[0,1],'Pick lists contain medication and inventory needs. Staff and equipment assignments are resource concepts, not those pick-list contents.')
q('OR100','Inventory',[105],'Compared with supply documentation, what additional information is characteristic of implant tracking?', ['Only the number of scheduled cases','Implant action, serial number, and expiration date','Only the surgeon login password','Only the scheduling block owner'],[1],'Implants require additional tracking such as action, serial number, and expiration date. Both supplies and implants can also require used and wasted quantities.')
q('OR100','Flowsheets',[122,123],'A nurse sees device values waiting to be filed. Why should those values be validated?', ['To review accuracy before filing to the chart','To automatically post the surgical log','To create a new preference card','To change the patient service'],[0],'Validation lets the clinician review device values before they enter the chart and avoids filing unnecessary data. It is not a charge-posting or scheduling function.')
