q('CLN251-252','Workflow Engine',[135],'A rule executes a matching directive that has no Continue Afterwards setting. What happens next?', ['Evaluation of that rule stops','The next condition is always evaluated','The system automatically moves to the next profile’s rule','All matching directives are merged'],[0],'Without Continue Afterwards, the system executes the matching directive and stops consulting that rule. Continued evaluation must be configured.')
q('CLN251-252','Workflow Engine',[135],'No condition in the Workflow Engine rule selected by the compiled profile matches the encounter. What is true?', ['A lower profile’s Workflow Engine rule is not automatically tried','Every lower-level rule is tried in sequence','The role record supplies a replacement navigator rule automatically','All profile rules run simultaneously'],[0],'Only the Workflow Engine rule selected by the compiled profile is used. A condition mismatch does not make the system fall through to another profile’s rule.')
q('CLN251-252','Workflow Engine',[135],'An analyst has built a Workflow Engine rule and must connect it to the user’s configuration. In which record is the rule linked?', ['Profile','Print group','Report','Category value'],[0],'Workflow Engine rules are linked in profiles. Reports and print groups present information, while category values define selectable field options.')
q('CLN251-252','Navigators',[152],'Which navigator record contains the section records used for documentation?', ['Topic','User template','Print group','Security class'],[0],'A navigator topic contains sections, and a navigator template can contain multiple topics. These navigator record types are all stored in LVN.')
q('CLN251-252','Navigators',[152],'An analyst changes a navigator topic’s caption to “Recovery Review.” Where does an end user see that text?', ['The navigator table of contents','The user’s login ID','The security-class name','The appointment status'],[0],'The topic caption supplies the display text in the navigator table of contents. It does not rename user credentials or scheduling statuses.')
q('CLN251-252','Roles',[169],'A user has four startup activities, two patient workspaces, and one Preference List Composer workspace open. How many workspaces count toward the total?', ['Three','Four','Six','Seven'],[1],'All startup activities together count as one workspace. Add two patient workspaces and one composer workspace: 1 + 2 + 1 = 4.')
q('CLN251-252','Roles',[169],'Which settings belong to a role record? Select all that apply.', ['Default startup activities','Maximum number of workspaces','Default login department','Order of Chart Review tabs'],[0,1],'The role controls startup activities and workspace limits. Default login department is an individual user setting; Chart Review tab order is configured through profiles.')
q('CLN251-252','Users and providers',[203],'A community referral physician never logs in to your Epic system. Which record arrangement matches this need?', ['A provider record can exist without a user record','A user record is required solely to receive referrals','A user template replaces the provider record','A role record replaces the provider record'],[0],'A referral physician can need a provider record without needing login access. User records are required for people who log in, and templates do not replace providers.')
q('CLN251-252','Users and providers',[203],'Which information is maintained for an individual user rather than as a shared user-template setting? Select all that apply.', ['Login ID','Default login department','Role for a group of similar users','Shared security classes'],[0,1],'Login ID and default login department are individual user settings. Roles and security classes can be shared through a user template for similar users.')
q('CLN251-252','Users and providers',[203],'True or false: A provider record may link directly to a shared user template instead of an individual user record.', ['True','False'],[1],'A provider can link to a user record, not directly to a user template. The individual user record can then obtain shared settings through its template.',kind='truefalse')
q('CLN251-252','Category lists',[226],'An analyst knows the display text of a field but needs to open its category list in maintenance. Which identifiers are required? Select all that apply.', ['Master-file INI','Item number','Every option synonym','The Text screen number'],[0,1],'The category list is identified by master-file INI and item number. Synonyms and the Text screen number are not the required address for the list.')
q('CLN251-252','Category lists',[226],'An obsolete category value already has production history. Which change preserves that history while retiring the option?', ['Deactivate the value','Delete the value','Reuse its ID for a different meaning','Change the master-file INI'],[0],'Deactivation preserves historical use. Deleting a value can erase its historical use, and reusing its identity for another meaning would misrepresent prior data.')
q('CLN251-252','Category lists',[226],'Category List Maintenance shows “Release Range: All Categories.” What does this indicate?', ['An Epic-controlled read-only system list','An unrestricted customer-controlled list','A list that must be deleted before editing','A list without historical values'],[0],'All Categories identifies an Epic-controlled system list that is read-only. It does not mean the customer can freely edit every value.')
q('OR350','Location configuration',[47],'System Definitions lists three Case Creation extensions. The location defines one extension for that same item. Which set applies at that location?', ['The location’s one extension','All four extensions automatically merged','Only the three system extensions','The most recently created extension regardless of level'],[0],'Case Extensions follows item-level override behavior. A populated location item overrides all system values for that item; it does not automatically append to them.')
q('OR350','Reporting configuration',[60],'System Definitions excludes weekend cases from a report calculation. A location needs weekends included. What should its Exclude Weekends setting be?', ['No','Yes','Blank to preserve the system setting','The same as Exclude Holidays'],[0],'Set Exclude Weekends to No at the location to override the system’s Yes. Leaving the field blank would retain the broader setting.')
q('OR350','Resource build',[99],'Which planned resources are represented by SER rather than an ORT resource-type record? Select all that apply.', ['Surgeons','Operating rooms','Generic circulator type','Generic equipment type'],[0,1],'Surgeons and operating rooms use SER records. Generic staff and equipment types use resource-type records, so ORT is not the planning record for surgeons or rooms.')
q('OR350','Resource build',[99],'A hospital needs a generic “Circulator” choice for case planning. What does the resource-type record describe?', ['The type of staff needed','One named nurse’s login credentials','A surgeon’s operating-room privileges','A room’s individual schedule'],[0],'A resource-type record describes a generic resource such as Circulator. Individual tracking and user login require other records; the resource type is not a person’s credentials.')
q('OR350','Room configuration',[145],'A room is absent from the Snapboard altogether. Which issues could explain that? Select all that apply.', ['The report is not configured to show the room','The room is not linked to an OR location','Its template lacks blocks','Its template contains private blocks'],[0,1],'Report inclusion and linkage to an OR location can explain a missing room. Missing or private blocks affect scheduling availability but do not by themselves make the room disappear.')
q('OR350','Room configuration',[145],'A room is visible and open, but a case cannot be scheduled into a block. Which restrictions could account for the mismatch? Select all that apply.', ['The block is reserved for another service','The block is reserved for another surgeon','The time is explicitly unblocked','The room is visible on the report'],[0,1],'Block allocation must match the applicable service or surgeon/surgeon group, or be unblocked. Visibility alone does not prove that a case is eligible for a reserved block.')
q('OR350','Room configuration',[145],'Which two components are needed for a fully configured operating room?', ['Room SER record and scheduling template','SUP record and balance record','User record and print group','Charge profile and preference list'],[0],'A room needs its SER record and scheduling template. Inventory and charging records serve different purposes and do not replace the room’s scheduling build.')
q('OR350','Inventory',[169],'The same supply needs different charging information at one inventory location. Where can that location-specific information be set?', ['Balance (BAL) record','Implant (IMP) record','User template','Navigator topic'],[0],'The BAL record supports location-specific charging information that differs from the SUP. IMP captures unique implant history rather than location-wide supply charging defaults.')
q('OR350','Inventory',[169],'Which record captures unique historical implant information from a procedure?', ['IMP','BAL','E2R','LVN'],[0],'The Implant (IMP) record captures implant documentation for tracking. BAL is for inventory balance/location information, while E2R and LVN serve user-interface configuration.')
q('OR350','Inventory',[169],'An organization receives many inventory-item definitions from its materials management system. Which tool helps create the corresponding item records?', ['Interface Item Mapping Tool','Preference List Composer','Session Information Report','Category List Maintenance'],[0],'The Interface Item Mapping Tool assists with creating inventory records from materials-management data. It is not a user-role or report-identification tool.')
q('OR350','Charging',[195],'A location normally uses one charge setup but needs exceptions for certain cases. What belongs in its charge profile? Select all that apply.', ['Default charge settings','Rules linked to alternative charge settings','A separate user password for each exception','A room scheduling template for each charge code'],[0,1],'A charge profile combines default settings with rules and alternative settings for exceptions. User passwords and room templates do not define charge-profile exceptions.')
q('OR350','Charging',[203],'A local charge table specifies one initial charge for the first 60 minutes and one additional charge per minute afterward. A log documents 72 minutes. How many additional per-minute units result?', ['12','11','60','72'],[0],'Under the stated table, 72 minus the 60-minute threshold yields 12 additional per-minute units. This arithmetic depends on the specified local setup, not a universal charging rule.')
q('OR350','Charging',[203],'Charges are unexpected and you need to identify the charge settings actually applied to a log. What is a useful investigation step?', ['Enable report/print-group assistance and inspect Charges to Be Sent','Change the user’s default department before investigating','Copy every charge code into a new table','Delete the log and schedule a replacement case'],[0],'The companion uses Session Information Report assistance and the Charges to Be Sent print group to identify applied charge settings. This provides evidence before changing configuration.')
q('OR350','Preference cards',[219],'A preference-card field is blank. Is it safe to assume every blank field inherits from the base procedure?', ['No; consult the field’s help text','Yes; inheritance is identical for every field','Yes; all blank fields merge every base value','No; blank fields can never inherit'],[0],'Some preference-card fields look to the base procedure when blank. The companion advises checking field help; neither universal inheritance nor universal non-inheritance is correct.')
q('OR350','Preference cards',[219],'A surgeon wants a particular nurse, but the preference card’s Staff and Equipment form lists generic resources. What kind of entries are these?', ['Resource types such as Circulator','Individual login IDs','Individual implant records','Patient contacts'],[0],'The form lists ORT resource types rather than individual people. A generic staffing requirement and a request for a particular person are different kinds of information.')
q('OR350','Procedure Pass',[244],'A task was created as Generic, but the team now wants a task type that automatically detects an active order. Can the existing task’s type simply be edited?', ['No; task type cannot be changed after creation','Yes; change its display caption','Yes; attach any charge profile','Yes; moving it to another location changes the type'],[0],'Task type is fixed after creation. Select or build an appropriate task of the required type instead of trying to change the type through unrelated settings.')
q('OR350','Procedure Pass',[244],'A prerequisite is satisfied as soon as a qualifying order is placed and active; completed results are not required. Which task type fits?', ['Presence of Orders','Procedure & Lab','Generic','Appointment'],[0],'Presence of Orders checks for placed active orders. Procedure & Lab addresses completion/results criteria; Generic is manually completed, and Appointment concerns scheduling/attendance.')
q('OR350','Procedure Pass',[264],'The same Procedure Pass configuration should affect all locations. Which broad configuration level does the course identify?', ['EMR System Definitions','A single user’s role','A single preference card','An individual room template'],[0],'EMR System Definitions is the broad setting identified for Procedure Pass across locations. A user role, card, or room template is not this system-wide configuration point.')
q('OR350','Procedure Pass',[264],'True or false: Every Procedure Pass rollout should start by building entirely new tasks, even when suitable tasks already exist.', ['True','False'],[1],'The course recommends using suitable pre-existing tasks whenever possible. Creating duplicates for every rollout adds maintenance without necessarily meeting a different need.',kind='truefalse')
q('OR350','SmartForms',[279],'A SmartForm should display a message when a component is clicked, but only if its value meets a condition. Which scripting sequence matches this?', ['Event → Condition → Action','Action → Release → Profile','Profile → Role → Print group','Condition → Inventory → Charge'],[0],'SmartForm scripting uses an event to trigger evaluation, an optional condition to test the situation, and an action to perform the response.')
q('OR350','SmartForms',[279],'An analyst has changed a SmartForm and wants the current version available to end users. Which steps fit? Select all that apply.', ['Check existing scripts for problems','Release the modified contact','Assume saving alone always releases it','Remove all scripts before any release'],[0,1],'Check Scripts helps identify scripting issues, and releasing the contact makes the current SmartForm version available. Saving and releasing are distinct, and scripts need not all be removed.')
q('OR350','Flowsheets',[293],'Which row-type and value-type combinations can be configured as a flowsheet trigger row? Select all that apply.', ['Data with Numeric Type','Custom Formula with Custom List','Data with Category Type','Data with a free-text string value'],[0,1,2],'Trigger rows require Data or Custom Formula as row type and Category Type, Custom List, or Numeric Type as value type. A free-text string value is outside that list.')
q('OR350','Flowsheets',[293],'A nurse repeatedly documents the same normal assessment values but must account for exceptions. Which feature supports that workflow?', ['A flowsheet macro followed by exception documentation','A room block','A charge-profile override','A category-list deletion'],[0],'A flowsheet macro can enter a common set of values quickly; clinicians then document exceptions. Scheduling and charging configuration do not perform assessment documentation.')
q('OR350','Security',[329],'True or false: Listing several OpTime Location security classes means all those location classes combine for every case.', ['True','False'],[1],'Only one OpTime Location security class affects the user at a time, selected according to where the case is scheduled. Listing several does not merge them for every case.',kind='truefalse')
